[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H10SG-329
TITLE: EMR: Clinical view - Disable treatment when patient’s plan is Inconsistent - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
This test case is designed to verify that the application displays an error message when the user attempts to load the plan into the external application.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
Create a patient and create a treatment plan for this patient with an Applicator size 1.5 cm. 

Ability to physically change target type. 

Description: 

This test case is designed to verify that the application displays an error message when the user attempts to load the plan into the external 
application.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1.Launch and login Heracles Internal 

2.Change Applicator to QC applicator. 

2.It the Patients tab, click the pre-created patient with the pre-created plan. 

3.Click the Approve button. 

1. open treatment tab 

4.Click the Load For Treatment button
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
The application shall not enable treatment delivery if the plan’s Applicator size differs from the actual Applicator type. 

The application shall present an error message when the user attempts to load the plan into the external application.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10SG-14
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H10SG-325
TITLE: EMR: Clinical view - Plan's Treatment Fields alert for inconsistency - (Alert -UI) - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
This test case verifies that appropriate alerts are displayed to the user when system conditions warrant notification. It validates the alert presentation and timing.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Launch and login Heracles internal 

2. Click the Physics tab 

3. Click the Applicator size Type and select Energy. 

4. Edit the dose rate 

5. Click Save 

6. Click Approve to approve the data. 

7. Return to patient record view. 

8. Select a field.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
The application should validate the treatment field parameters fetched from the DB, including duration and dose, and alert the user that the 
values in the prescription are inconsistent with the calculated parameters.
<<<
