[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H10SG-750
TITLE: System logs’ view - Layout - Search Functionality Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
This test case verifies the layout and user interface components of the System logs’ view. It validates that all UI elements are properly displayed and arranged according to specifications.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Click the Log tab in the application navigation menu 

2. Click on the Search edit control at the top of the interface 

3. Enter a specific search term (e.g., "user") 

4. Observe the log list view results 

5. Verify that only log entries containing the search term are displayed 

6. Clear the search box and enter a different search term (e.g., "Admin") 

7. Click the Search button 

8. Verify that the results update to show only entries matching the new search term 

9. Clear the search box completely 

10. Verify that all log entries are displayed (no filter applied) 

11. Enter a search term that has no matches (e.g., "xyz123nonexistent") 

12. Verify appropriate handling (empty list or "no results" message)
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
• The search box accepts text input 

• Search results display only log entries matching the search term) 

• Search looks through all relevant fields (Time, Status, Type, Record) 

• Clearing the search term and searching displays all log entries 

• Search with no matches displays an empty list or appropriate message 

• Search results update dynamically based on the search term 

• The list view refreshes correctly after each search operation
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10SG-67
  ROLE: Verifies

