[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H10SG-778
TITLE: Load For Treatment - Resume Uncompleted Treatment - UI Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
This test case verifies the functionality and operation of Load For Treatment. It validates that the component behaves according to specifications and system requirements.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Click the Patients tab in the application navigation menu 

2. Double-click on the patient with uncompleted treatment 

3. Click the Treatments tab 

4. Select the field/site with the uncompleted treatment (e.g., "Field 0 - BCC") 

5. Verify that the treatment history shows at least one treatment marked as "Partial" or incomplete 

6. Click the Load For Treatment button at the bottom right of the interface 

7. Verify that an alert dialog appears with the title "Uncompleted Treatment Plan" 

8. Verify that the alert message states: 

o 

"The latest treatment plan delivery was not completed. You can load the remaining treatment or a whole treatment." 

9. Verify that the alert provides options (buttons) such as: 

o Load remaining treatment 

o Load complete treatment 

o Close/Cancel 

10. Click Load remaining treatment (or equivalent option) 

11. Verify that the system sends the remaining uncompleted plan to the external application 

12. Verify that the external application is triggered/notified that a plan is pending for load 

13. Verify that the external application recalculates the treatment time according to the latest treatment completion status 

14. Alternatively, go back to step 6 and click Load complete treatment option 

15. Verify that the system sends the complete treatment plan to the external application 

16. Verify proper notification/confirmation of successful plan loading
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. The Load For Treatment button is visible and accessible in the Treatments view 

2. Clicking Load For Treatment triggers validation of the treatment completion status 

3. An alert dialog appears when an uncompleted treatment plan is detected 

4. The alert clearly informs the user that the latest treatment was not completed 

5. The alert provides clear options to load either the remaining treatment or the whole treatment 

6. Clicking "Load remaining treatment" sends only the uncompleted portions to the external app 

7. Clicking "Load complete treatment" sends the entire treatment plan to the external app 

8. The external application is properly triggered and receives the plan data 

9. The external application recalculates treatment time based on the completion status 

10. Remaining treatment time reflects only undelivered portions 

11. Complete treatment time reflects the full prescribed plan 

12. The user receives confirmation when the plan is successfully loaded 

13. Clicking Close/Cancel dismisses the alert without loading the plan
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10SG-422
  ROLE: Verifies

