[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H10SG-749
TITLE: Service - System's Signals - UI Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
This test case verifies the functionality and operation of Service. It validates that the component behaves according to specifications and system requirements.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Click the Service tab in the application navigation menu 

2. Verify that the Service interface loads and displays the system signals dashboard 

3. Locate and verify the System section displays the following parameters: 

o System State 

o System Runtime [ms] 

o System Fault Flags [raw] 

o 

Interlock Flags [raw] 

4. Locate and verify the General section displays the following parameters: 

o Ring LED State 

o Base LED State 

o Applicator ID (1) [Raw] 

o Applicator ID (2) [Raw] 

o Buttons [Raw] 

5. Locate and verify the Operational points section displays: 

o Current Point 

o Total Points 

6. Locate and verify the Timers section displays the following parameters: 

o 

o 

Internal Timer State 

Internal Timer Value [sec] 

o Timer 1 State 

o Timer 1 Value [sec] 

o Timer 2 State 

o Timer 2 Value [sec] 

7. Locate and verify the Coils section displays the following parameters: 

o X coil current [mA] 

o Y coil current [mA] 

o Focus current [mA] 

8. Locate and verify the HVPS (High Voltage Power Supply) section displays: 

o HVPS Runtime [ms] 

o HVPS IO [Raw] 

o HVPS Status Flags [Raw] 

o kV Feedback [kV] 

o mA Feedback [mA] 

o Filament setpoint [mA] 

o Filament feedback [mA] 

o Grid setpoint [V] 

o Grid feedback [V] 

9. Locate and verify the Ion pump section displays: 

o 

Ion pump voltage [V] 

10. Locate and verify the Cooling system section displays: 

o Water pressure [PSI] 

o Water Flow [LPM] 

o Water temperature [°C] 

o HeatSink temperature [°C] 

o Peltier temperature [°C] 

o Cabinet temperature [°C] 

11. Locate and verify the Magnetometers section displays: 

o Mag 1 X [μT] 

o Mag 1 Y [μT] 

o Mag 1 Z [μT] 

o Mag 2 X [μT] 

o Mag 2 Y [μT] 

o Mag 2 Z [μT] 

12. Observe the displayed values for 30-60 seconds to verify that the signals update in real-time 

13. Trigger a system state change (if possible) and verify that the displayed values reflect the change
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
• The Service tab is accessible and loads without errors 

