[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H10SG-762
TITLE: Patients - Simulation View - Add Patient’s Prescription - UI Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
This test case verifies the creation and addition of new items in the system. It validates the complete workflow from initiation through successful data persistence.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Click the Patients tab in the application navigation menu 

2. Locate the pre-defined patient in the patient list 

3. Double-click on the patient entry to open the patient's Simulation View 

4. 

In the left panel, click on the pre-defined simulation entry (e.g., "Field 1 BCC" or the relevant simulation field) 

5. Verify that the simulation details are displayed in the center panel 

6. Locate the Prescription section in the right panel of the interface 

7. Verify that the Prescription section contains the following fields: 

o Energy [kV] (dropdown) 

o Dose Per Fx [cGy] (editable field) 

o Fx per week (dropdown) 

o TDF (dropdown) 

o Number of Fx (editable field) 

o Total Dose [cGy] (non-editable/calculated field) 

o Duration [s] (field) 

8. Click the Add button in the Prescription section (bottom right area with Reload, Add, and Save buttons) 

9. Verify that all prescription fields are cleared and ready for new data entry 

10. Click on the Energy [kV] dropdown and select an energy value (e.g., "50" or available option) 

11. In the Dose Per Fx [cGy] field, enter a decimal value (e.g., "200.0") 

12. Click on the Fx per week dropdown and select a frequency value (e.g., "2") 

13. Click on the TDF dropdown and select a TDF value from the available options (e.g. 95) 

14. In the Number of Fx field, enter an integer value (e.g., "25") 

15. Verify that the Total Dose [cGy] field automatically calculates and displays the result of [Dose Per Fx] × [Number of Fx] 

16. Verify that the Total Dose field is non-editable (read-only) 

17. In the Duration [s] field, enter the treatment duration value (if required) 

18. Click the Save button to save the new prescription 

19. Verify that the prescription is saved and associated with the selected simulation 

20. Verify that the prescription data persists when navigating away and returning to the simulation 

Expected behavior 

• Energy dropdown displays available energy options and allows selection 

• Dose Per Fx field accepts decimal numbers 

• Fx per week dropdown displays options 1-7 and allows selection 

• TDF dropdown displays available TDF options and allows selection 

• Number of Fx field accepts integer numbers only 

• Total Dose [cGy] automatically calculates as [Dose Per Fx] × [Number of Fx] 

• Calculation updates immediately when either Dose Per Fx or Number of Fx changes 

• Total Dose field is non-editable (read-only/disabled) 

• Calculated value is accurate 

• The Save button successfully saves the new prescription 

• The prescription is associated with the correct patient and simulation 

• All entered data is saved accurately 

• The prescription persists after navigating away and returning
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
• Energy dropdown displays available energy options and allows selection 

• Dose Per Fx field accepts decimal numbers 

• Fx per week dropdown displays options 1-7 and allows selection 

• TDF dropdown displays available TDF options and allows selection 

• Number of Fx field accepts integer numbers only 

• Total Dose [cGy] automatically calculates as [Dose Per Fx] × [Number of Fx] 

• Calculation updates immediately when either Dose Per Fx or Number of Fx changes 

• Total Dose field is non-editable (read-only/disabled) 

• Calculated value is accurate 

• The Save button successfully saves the new prescription 

• The prescription is associated with the correct patient and simulation 

• All entered data is saved accurately 

• The prescription persists after navigating away and returning
<<<
