[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H10SG-783
TITLE: Patients - Simulation View - Auto-Calculation Field Size - UI Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
This test case verifies automatic calculations and computations. It validates that calculated values are accurate and match expected results based on input parameters.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Click the Patients tab in the application navigation menu 

2. Double-click on a patient to open the Simulation View 

3. Click the Simulation tab 

4. Select a field/simulation from the sites list (e.g., "Field 3 - BCC") 

5. Locate the Simulation section with Lesion Size, Margin Size, and Field Size fields 

6. Enter values in the Lesion Size [cm] fields: 

o First box (X dimension): Enter "5.1" 

o Second box (Y dimension): Enter "5.9" 

7. Enter values in the Margin Size [cm] fields: 

o First box (X dimension): Enter "0.1" 

o Second box (Y dimension): Enter "0.1" 

8. Verify that the Field Size [cm] automatically calculates using the formula: 

o Field Size X = Lesion Size X + (2 × Margin Size X) 

o Field Size Y = Lesion Size Y + (2 × Margin Size Y) 

o Expected X: 5.1 + (2 × 0.1) = 5.3 cm 

o Expected Y: 5.9 + (2 × 0.1) = 6.1 cm 

9. Verify that the calculated Field Size displays: "5.3 x 6.1" (or as per actual calculation) 

10. Modify the Lesion Size X to "1.0" and Lesion Size Y to "1.0" 

11. Modify the Margin Size X to "0.5" and Margin Size Y to "0.5" 

12. Verify that Field Size recalculates: 

o Expected X: 1.0 + (2 × 0.5) = 2.0 cm 

o Expected Y: 1.0 + (2 × 0.5) = 2.0 cm 

o Field Size should display: "2.0 x 2.0" 

13. Test with different values - Lesion: "3.0 x 4.0", Margin: "1.0 x 0.5" 

14. Verify Field Size calculates correctly: 

o Expected X: 3.0 + (2 × 1.0) = 5.0 cm 

o Expected Y: 4.0 + (2 × 0.5) = 5.0 cm 

15. Verify that the Field Size fields are non-editable (read-only/calculated fields) 

16. Click the Save button to save the simulation data 

17. Navigate away and return to verify that Field Size persists correctly
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
• Lesion Size fields accept numeric decimal input (two fields for X and Y dimensions) 

• Margin Size fields accept numeric decimal input (two fields for X and Y dimensions) 

• Field Size automatically calculates when Lesion Size or Margin Size values are entered or modified 

• Field Size calculation uses the correct formula: Field Size = Lesion Size + (2 × Margin Size) 

• Field Size X calculation: Lesion Size X + (2 × Margin Size X) 

• Field Size Y calculation: Lesion Size Y + (2 × Margin Size Y) 

• Calculated Field Size displays with appropriate decimal precision 

• Field Size fields are non-editable (read-only/calculated) 

• Field Size updates immediately when Lesion Size or Margin Size changes 

• Saved Field Size values persist after navigation
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10SG-740
  ROLE: Verifies

