o Columns: Permission categories (Patient's Clinical Data, Patient's Treatment, System Calibration, Quality Assurance, System 

Settings, User Management, Services) 

6. Verify that each intersection contains a checkbox to set/unset permissions 

7. Verify the current permission states (checked/unchecked) 

o e.g. Administrator: All permissions checked 

8. Click on an unchecked checkbox to set permission (e.g., enable "System Settings" for RTT role) 

9. Verify that the checkbox becomes checked 

10. Click on a checked checkbox to unset a permission (e.g., disable "Patient's Treatment" for RTT role) 

11. Verify that the checkbox becomes unchecked 

