[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H10SG-751
TITLE: System logs’ view - Layout - Date Range Filtering UI Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
This test case verifies the layout and user interface components of the System logs’ view. It validates that all UI elements are properly displayed and arranged according to specifications.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Click the Log tab in the application navigation menu 

2. Observe the default date range displayed in the calendar control 

3. Click on the Calendar control 

4. Select a specific start date (e.g., Oct 22, 2025) 

5. Select a specific end date (e.g., Oct 24, 2025) 

6. Click the Apply button 

7. Verify that the selected date range is displayed in the calendar control 

8. Observe the log entries in the list view 

9. Verify that only log entries within the selected date range are displayed 

10. Change the date range to a single day 

11. Verify that only entries from that specific day are displayed 

12. Change the date range to include future dates 

13. Reset the date range to include all available log entries 

14. Verify that all log entries are displayed again
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
• The calendar control is interactive and allows date selection 

• Users can select both start and end dates 

• The selected date range is clearly displayed 

• Log entries are filtered to show only those within the selected time frame 

• Entries outside the selected date range are not displayed 

• The list view updates automatically when the date range changes 

• Date range selection persists until changed by the user 

• Single-day selection displays only entries from that day
<<<
