[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H10SG-770
TITLE: Patients - Treatment View - View Treatment Details - UI Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
This test case verifies the functionality and operation of Patients. It validates that the component behaves according to specifications and system requirements.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Click the Patients tab in the application navigation menu 

2. Double-click on the patient with treatment history 

3. 

In the left panel, click on a field entry from the simulation sites list (e.g., "Field 4 - BCC") 

4. Click the Treatments sub-tab at the top of the view 

5. Verify that the treatment history table is displayed with multiple treatment records 

6. Locate a treatment entry in the history table (e.g., Fx: 1, Date: 10/19/2025 10:26:16 PM) 

7. Click the Details button (e.g. play icon) for the selected treatment in the rightmost column 

8. Verify that a treatment details panel expands or opens displaying additional information 

9. Verify the treatment details section displays the following fields with their values: 

o Actual Duration [sec]: e.g., "0" 

o Actual Dose [cGy]: e.g., "50" 

o Current [mA]: e.g., "4" 

10. Click the Details button for a different treatment record (e.g., Fx: 2) 

11. Verify that the details panel updates to show information for the newly selected treatment
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
• The Details button (e.g. play icon) is visible and clickable for each treatment record 

• Clicking the Details button opens/expands a treatment details panel 

• The details panel header displays the Fx number and Date of the selected treatment 

• The treatment details section displays three fields: Actual Duration [sec], Actual Dose [cGy], and Current [mA] 

• All values are displayed accurately and match the stored treatment data 

• Clicking Details for different treatments updates the panel with the correct corresponding data
<<<
