[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H10SG-763
TITLE: Patients - Simulation View - Add Patient’s Prescription - UI Field Validation Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
This test case verifies the creation and addition of new items in the system. It validates the complete workflow from initiation through successful data persistence.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Click the Patients tab in the application navigation menu 

2. Double-click on the patient to open the Simulation View 

3. 

In the left panel, click on a simulation entry 

4. Click the Add button in the Prescription section to add a new prescription 

5. Attempt to enter non-numeric text (e.g., "abc") in the Dose Per Fx [cGy] field 

6. Verify the system's response (should reject or clear invalid input) 

7. Attempt to enter non-numeric text in the Number of Fx field 

8. Verify the system's response (should reject or clear invalid input) 

9. Attempt to enter a decimal number (e.g., "25.5") in the Number of Fx field 

10. Verify that the system either rejects the decimal or rounds to an integer 

11. Enter a negative number (e.g., "-10") in the Dose Per Fx [cGy] field 

12. Verify that the system rejects negative values 

13. Enter a negative number in the Number of Fx field 

14. Verify that the system rejects negative values 

15. Enter "0" in the Dose Per Fx [cGy] field 

16. Enter "10" in the Number of Fx field 

17. Verify that Total Dose calculates as "0.0" cGy 

18. Attempt to manually edit the Total Dose [cGy] field 

19. Verify that the field is non-editable (read-only/disabled) 

20. Fill in only some fields (e.g., only Energy and Dose Per Fx) and click Save 

21. Verify that the system indicates which required fields are missing 

22. Verify that the Fx per week dropdown only displays values 1-7 

23. Enter valid data in all fields and click Save 

24. Verify that the prescription is saved successfully
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
• Dose Per Fx field accepts only numeric values (integers and decimals) 

• Number of Fx field accepts only integer values (whole numbers) 

• Non-numeric input is rejected or prevented in numeric fields 

• Decimal values are rejected or rounded in the Number of Fx field 

• Negative values are rejected in Dose Per Fx and Number of Fx fields 

• Fx per week dropdown displays only values 1-7 

• Values outside acceptable ranges are rejected 

• Save button is disabled or validation prevents saving incomplete data 

Observed behavior 

As expected. 

Need a better message when entering a non-numeric number. (instead of e could not converted)
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10SG-80
  ROLE: Verifies

