UID: TC-H10SG-261
TITLE: EMR: Patient's Clinical Data View - View Patient Prescription - DB Communication Error - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
Verify that the application presents the user with a warning message when the retrieval of a patient's prescription fails due to a communication error with the database.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
This test case requires the ability to intentionally create a communication error with the database. 

The test uses a special version of the application that artificially receives communication errors from the DB when fetching 
prescriptions.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1.Launch and login Heracles internal SW 

2.Navigate to the patients’ tab 

3. Verify that a patient with the following details exists in the system or create a new patient by pressing "New patient" and filing the 
following details: 

First Name: FirstNameTest 

Middle Name: MiddleNameTest 

Last Name: LastNameTest 

Sex: Male 

DOB: 01/01/1980 

MRN:12345 

4. Click the "Save Patient" button at the bottom of the registration form. 

5. In the patients list view, click twice on the newly created patient. 

6.Navigate to "Plan" tab and click the "Add" button at the bottom of the plan tab on the bottom left corner of the screen. 

7. Fill in the following details: 

Site Name: testSite 

Pathology: testPathology 

8. Click the "Save" button. 

9. In the same plan tab under "Simulation" click the "Add" button. 

10.Fill in the following details for "Simulation": 

\*Lesion Size[cm]:1.00 x 1.00 

\*Margin Size[cm]:1.00 

\*Sheild Size [cm]: 1.00 

\*Lesion Depth [mm]: 1.00 

\*Position: Prone (Select from the Position drop-down menu) 

\*Device :HeadHolder (select HeadHolder from the drop-down menu) 

11.Click the "Save" button under "Simulation". 

12.In the same plan tab, click the "Add" button under "Prescription". 

13. Fill in the following details: 

Does Pre Fx [cGy]: 1 

TDF: 92(select from the drop-down menu) 

Fx per week: Select 1 from the drop-down menu. 

Number of Fx: 1 

Energy [kV]: 10 (Select from the drop-down menu) 

14. Click the "Add" prescription button and save. 

12.Exit the application by navigating the Exit tab and clicking exit. 

Exit the application and run the testing version of Heracles internal SW, which artificially returns a DB connection error when 
fetching the prescription. 

13. Re-Launch and login the application. 

14. In the patient tab click the patient you have created earlier. 

15.Click the Site Name: testSite in the plan tab on the right side.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
16.The application shall present the user with a warning message when retrieving a patient’s prescription fails due to a communication error 
with the database. The message should ask the user to retry after a few seconds.
<<<
