[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H10SG-780
TITLE: Settings - Users Authorization Management - Create New Role - UI Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
This test case verifies the creation and addition of new items in the system. It validates the complete workflow from initiation through successful data persistence.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Log in to the application with administrator credentials 

2. Click the Settings tab in the application navigation menu 

3. Click the User Permissions sub-tab 

4. Verify that the permissions matrix displays existing roles (Administrator, RTT, Physicist, Service) 

5. Click the New Role button at the bottom left 

6. Verify that a role creation panel opens on the right side 

7. 

In the Role field, enter a custom role name (e.g., "test" or "Custom_Role") 

8. 

In the Permissions section, select specific permissions by checking the appropriate checkboxes: 

o Check "Services" 

o Optionally check other permissions (e.g., "Quality Assurance") 

9. Leave other permissions unchecked to create a role with limited access 

10. Click the Save button at the bottom right of the panel 

11. Verify that a success confirmation appears (if applicable) 

12. Verify that the new role appears in the permissions matrix table with the assigned permissions 

13. Verify that the new role row displays: 

o Role name: "test" 

o Services: ✓ (checked) 

o All other permissions: unchecked 

14. Click the X button to close the role creation panel 

15. Navigate away from the User Permissions tab and return 

16. Verify that the newly created role persists in the permissions matrix
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
• Clicking New Role opens a role creation panel 

• The panel contains a Role name field and a Permissions checklist 

• The Role field accepts text input for custom role names 

• All available permissions are listed as checkboxes 

• Multiple permissions can be selected by checking the appropriate boxes 

• The Save button successfully creates a new role 

• The new role appears in the permissions matrix immediately after creation 

• The role displays with the correct name and assigned permissions 

• Only the selected permissions are checked for the new role 

• The new role persists after navigating away and returning 

• The new role becomes available in the User Management role dropdown 

• Users can be assigned to the newly created custom role
<<<
