[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H10SG-769
TITLE: Patients - Treatments view - Layout - UI Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
This test case verifies the layout and user interface components of the Patients. It validates that all UI elements are properly displayed and arranged according to specifications.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Click the Patients tab in the application navigation menu 

2. Locate and click twice on the patient with treatment history to pen its simulation view. 

3. Click the Treatments sub-tab to view the treatment history 

4. Verify the patient demographic data is displayed at the top of the view. 

5. Verify the master-details layout is displayed with: 

o Master view: Sites/fields list on the left panel 

o Details view: Treatment information on the right panel 

6. Verify the sites list (master view) displays all available fields with: 

o Field number and name (e.g., "Field 5") 

o Pathology type (e.g., "BCC") 

7. Click on a field entry (e.g., "Field 5") in the sites list 

8. Verify the details’ view displays the following sections: 

Simulation Data Section: 

• Lesion Size [cm]: Two values (e.g., "9.8 x 5.9") 

• Margin Size [cm]: Two values (e.g., "0.1 x 0.1") 

• Field Size [cm]: Two calculated values (e.g., "0.2 x 0.2") 

• Applicator size: Dropdown showing selected value (e.g., "1.5 cm") 

• Lesion Depth [mm]: Value (e.g., "12.5") 

• Devices: List of devices (e.g., "Head Holder") 

• Positions: Selected position (e.g., "Laying on LEFT Side") 

• Notes: Text field (e.g., "Allergy to metals") 

Prescription Data Section: 

• Fx per week: Value (e.g., "2") 

• Number of Fx: Value (e.g., "6") 

• Energy [kV]: Value (e.g., "50") 

• TDF: Value (e.g., "100") 

• Dose Per Fx [cGy]: Value (e.g., "600.00") 

• Total Dose [cGy]: Calculated value (e.g., "3600") 

• Duration [s]: Value (e.g., "60") 

• Actual Dose [cGy]: Value (e.g., "600") 

1. Verify the Treatments section displays treatment summary: 

o Total Fraction: e.g., "1 / 6" 

o Total Dose Delivered [cGy]: e.g., "600 / 3600" 

2. Verify the treatments table displays with the following column headers: 

o Fx 

o Date 

o Lesion Depth 

o Energy [kV] 

o Daily Dose [cGy] 

o Cumulative Dose [cGy] 

o Details 

3. Verify the treatment record(s) in the table display correct information: 

o Fx: Fraction number (e.g., "1") 

o Date: Treatment date and time (e.g., "10/19/2025 10:26:16 PM") 

o Lesion Depth: Measured depth (e.g., "12.5") 

o Energy [kV]: Delivered energy (e.g., "50") 

o Daily Dose [cGy]: Delivered dose (e.g., "600") 

o Cumulative Dose [cGy]: Running total (e.g., "600") 

o Details: Play button/link to view details 

4. Verify clicking on different fields in the sites list updates the details view accordingly
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
• The Treatments tab opens successfully and displays the treatment history view 

• Patient demographic data is clearly visible at the top 

• Master-details layout is properly implemented with sites list on the left 

• All fields in the sites list are displayed and selectable 

• Prescription data section displays all prescription fields with accurate values 

• Treatment summary shows total fractions and total dose delivered 

• Treatments table displays all column headers correctly 

• Each treatment record shows complete information including Fx number, Date, Lesion Depth, Energy, Daily Dose, Cumulative 

Dose, and Details link 

• All data is accurate and matches the stored treatment records 

• Clicking different sites/fields updates the details view appropriately 

• Details button/link is functional for viewing individual treatment details
<<<
