[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H10SG-774
TITLE: Physics - Alert for unsaved data - UI Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
This test case verifies that appropriate alerts are displayed to the user when system conditions warrant notification. It validates the alert presentation and timing.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Click the Physics tab in the application navigation menu 

2. Select an Applicator Type (e.g., "1.5 cm") and Energy Level [kV] (e.g., "50") 

3. Modify a value in any field (e.g., change CMF 2,3 from "1" to "5") 

4. Verify that the Save button becomes enabled (indicating unsaved changes) 

5. Without clicking Save, attempt to navigate away by clicking on another tab (e.g., Patients, Log, Settings, or Service) 

6. Verify that an alert or confirmation dialog appears warning about unsaved data 

7. Click Cancel or No in the alert dialog 

8. Verify that navigation is prevented and the user remains on the Physics view 

9. Verify that the modified data is still present in the fields 

10. Attempt to navigate away and click Discard (or similar) 

11. Verify that navigation proceeds without saving and changes are discarded
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
• An alert or confirmation dialog appears when attempting to navigate away with unsaved changes 

• The alert message clearly indicates that there are unsaved changes 

• The alert provides options such as: Cancel/No 

• Clicking Cancel/No prevents navigation and keeps the user on the Physics view 

• Unsaved data remains in the fields after canceling navigation 

• No data loss occurs when the user chooses to save 

• The alert appears consistently for all navigation attempts (clicking different tabs)
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10SG-118
  ROLE: Verifies

