[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H10SG-782
TITLE: Patients - Simulation View - Auto-Calculation of Emission Duration - UI Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
This test case verifies automatic calculations and computations. It validates that calculated values are accurate and match expected results based on input parameters.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Click the Physics tab in the application navigation menu 

2. Select Applicator Type: "1.5 cm" from the dropdown 

3. Select Energy Level [kV]: "70" from the dropdown 

4. Locate the Dose Rate section and note the configured value (e.g., "600.00 cGy/Min") 

5. Click the Patients tab to navigate to patient management 

6. Double-click on a patient to open the Simulation View 

7. Click the Simulation tab 

8. Select a field/simulation from the sites list (e.g., "Field 2 - BCC") 

9. Verify the Simulation section shows: 

o Applicator size: "1.5 cm" (matching Physics configuration) 

10. Verify the Prescription section shows: 

o Energy [kV]: "70" (matching Physics configuration) 

o Dose Per Fx [cGy]: "300.00" 

11. Locate the Duration [s] field in the Prescription section 

12. Verify that the Duration is automatically calculated using the formula: 

o Duration [sec] = (Dose Per Fx [cGy] / Dose Rate [cGy/min]) × 60 

o Expected: (300.00 / 600.00) × 60 = 30.0 seconds 

13. Verify that the calculated Duration value is displayed: "30" or "30.0" 

14. Modify the Dose Per Fx [cGy] to a different value (e.g., "450.00") 

15. Verify that the Duration automatically recalculates: 

o Expected: (450.00 / 600.00) × 60 = 45.0 sec 

16. Test minimum resolution by entering a dose that results in a fractional duration (e.g., "325.00") 

17. Verify that the Duration displays with at least 0.1 second resolution: 

o Expected: (325.00 / 600.00) × 60 = 32.5 seconds
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
• The Duration [s] field automatically calculates based on Dose Per Fx and Dose Rate 

• The calculation uses the correct formula: Duration = (Dose Per Fx / Dose Rate) × 60 

• The calculated duration is accurate for the given dose and dose rate 

• Duration automatically recalculates when Dose Per Fx is modified 

• The calculation displays with minimum resolution of 0.1 seconds 

• Fractional durations (e.g., 32.5 seconds) are properly displayed 

• The duration field updates immediately when dose values change 

• The calculation is consistent and accurate across different dose values 

• No rounding errors occur in the calculation
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10SG-739
  ROLE: Verifies

