[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H10SG-773
TITLE: Physics - Import configuration from CSV file - Improper formatting in the CSV - UI Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
This test case verifies data import/export functionality. It validates that data can be properly exchanged between the system and external formats.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Click the Physics tab in the application navigation menu 

2. Verify that the Physics configuration interface is displayed 

3. Click on the Import from CSV text field or upload button 

4. Browse and select the CSV file with improper formatting from the filesystem 

5. Attempt to import the file by clicking the upload/import button 

6. Verify that the system validates the CSV file format 

7. Verify that an error alert or message is displayed indicating improper formatting 

8. Verify that the error message provides information about the formatting issue (e.g., "Invalid CSV format", "Missing required 

columns") 

9. Verify that the import process fails and no data is imported into the physics configuration 

10. Verify that existing physics data remains unchanged 

11. Click OK or dismiss the error message 

12. Verify that the user can attempt to import another file
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
• The system validates CSV file format during the import process 

• The error message clearly indicates that the CSV file has improper formatting 

• The import process fails and does not proceed with improperly formatted data 

• No invalid or partial data is imported into the system 

• Existing physics configuration data remains unchanged and uncorrupted 

• The user can dismiss the error and attempt to import a different file 

• The system prevents data corruption by rejecting improperly formatted files
<<<
