[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H10SG-775
TITLE: Physics - Import configuration from CSV file - UI Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
This test case verifies data import/export functionality. It validates that data can be properly exchanged between the system and external formats.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Click the Physics tab in the application navigation menu 

2. Verify that the Physics configuration interface is displayed 

3. Click on the Import from CSV text field or browse button 

4. Navigate to and select the properly formatted CSV file from the filesystem 

5. Click the upload/import button to initiate the import process 

6. Verify that the system processes the CSV file 

7. Verify that the Magnetometer Corrections - Correction Matrix fields are populated with imported data 

8. Verify that the Magnetometer Corrections - Reference Field fields are populated with imported data 

9. Verify that the Coils section fields are populated with imported data 

10. Verify that the Heater Current [mA] field is populated with the imported value 

11. Verify that the Dose Rate [cGy/Min] field is populated with the imported value 

12. Click the Save button to save the imported configuration 

13. Navigate away and return to the Physics tab to verify data persistence
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
• The Import from CSV control is functional and allows file selection 

• The system successfully processes the properly formatted CSV file 

• All imported data populates the corresponding fields correctly: 

o All 12 Magnetometer Correction Matrix fields are populated 

o All 6 Reference Field values are populated 

o All 3 Coils values (X, Y, Focus) are populated 

o Heater Current value is populated 

o Dose Rate value is populated 

• All imported values match the data in the CSV file 

• The Save button is enabled after import (indicating changes) 

• 

Imported data can be saved successfully 

• All imported and saved data persists after navigation
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10SG-115
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H10SG-784
TITLE: Main View - System Status - UI Test
STATEMENT: >>>
This test case verifies system status and monitoring capabilities. It validates that system state information is accurately displayed and updated.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
• The application is installed and launched successfully 

• User is logged in with appropriate privileges 

• The system is connected to the applicator hardware and actively receiving telemetry data 

1. Log in to the application with valid credentials 

2. Verify that a System Status panel is visible on the screen (typically on the left or right side) 

3. Verify that the System Status panel displays the following information fields: 

o System status: Current status indicator 

o Energy [kV]: Energy level field 

o Timer [Sec]: Emission time field 

o Emission [mA]: Emission current field 

4. Verify that the System status field displays the current state (e.g., "NoComm", "Ready", "Irradiating", "Error") 

5. Verify that system error indicators are displayed when applicable (e.g., red error icon with "Applicator" message) 

6. Verify that the Energy [kV] field displays the current or configured energy level 

7. Verify that the Timer [Sec] field displays: 

1. "0" or empty when system is idle 

2. Countdown time when system is irradiating 

8. Verify that the Emission [mA] field displays the current emission current value 

9. Navigate to different tabs (Patients, Log, Physics, Settings) 

10. Verify that the System Status panel remains visible on all screens/tabs 

11. Verify that additional status indicators are present: 

o Radiation symbol/icon (visible when applicable) 

o System status message: "System not ready" or "Applicator" with appropriate icon 

o 

Information (i) and settings icons at the bottom 

12. initiate a treatment simulation 

13. Verify that during emission: 

o System status changes to "Irradiating" or equivalent 

o Timer counts down from the prescribed duration 

o Energy [kV] displays the delivery energy 

o Emission [mA] displays the actual emission current 

14. Verify that status updates occur in real-time 

15. Test with system errors (if possible): 

o Disconnect applicator 

o Verify error status is displayed 

o Verify appropriate error messages appear
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
• The System Status panel is visible and accessible at all times 

• The panel displays four key fields: System status, Energy [kV], Timer [Sec], and Emission [mA] 

• System status field accurately reflects the current system state (NoComm, Ready, Irradiating, Error, etc.) 

• System errors are clearly indicated with appropriate icons and messages 

• Energy level is displayed 

• Timer displays countdown during emission/irradiation 

• Emission current is displayed during active emission 

• The System Status panel persists across all application views and tabs 

• Status information updates in real-time during system operation 

• Visual indicators (radiation symbol, status icons) are present 

• Additional status messages ("System not ready", "Applicator") display when relevant 

• The panel provides clear and immediate feedback about system state 

• All status information is accurate and synchronized with actual system state
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10SG-54
  ROLE: Verifies

