[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H10SG-759
TITLE: User Profile Management - Delete UI Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
This test case verifies the deletion or removal of items from the system. It validates that removal is properly executed and reflected in the application.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Log in to the application as the administrator user 

2. Click the Settings tab in the application navigation menu 

3. Click the User Management tab 

4. Verify that the user list displays both the administrator and non-administrator users 

5. Click on the non-administrator user entry in the user list to select it 

6. Click the Delete button at the bottom of the interface 

7. Verify that a confirmation dialog appears asking to confirm the deletion 

8. Click Confirm or Yes in the confirmation dialog 

9. Verify that the non-administrator user is removed from the user list 

10. Verify that a success confirmation message appears (if applicable) 

11. Verify that only the administrator user remains in the user list (or other users if multiple exist) 

Expected behavior 

• The User Management interface displays all existing users 

• Confirming the deletion removes the user account from the system 

• The user list updates immediately to reflect the deletion 

• The deleted user no longer appears in the user list 

• The deleted user account cannot be used to log in to the system
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
• The User Management interface displays all existing users 

• Confirming the deletion removes the user account from the system 

• The user list updates immediately to reflect the deletion 

• The deleted user no longer appears in the user list 

• The deleted user account cannot be used to log in to the system
<<<
