[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H10SG-264
TITLE: EMR: Patient's Clinical Data View - Save Patient Plan - DB Communication Error - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
Verify that the application presents the user with a warning message when saving a new plan fails due to a communication error with the database
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
A patient with an existing simulation.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Launch Heracles internal SW 

2. Navigate to the patient’s tab 

3. Navigate to the "Simulation" tab in the patient record. 

4. 

Click Add, to add Prescription fields. 

5. Create an intended communication error with the database to prevent it from saving a new patient's treatment plan (Shutdown 

database service). 

6. Click the save button to save the new plan. 

7. Restore the DBService 

8. Click Retry.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
6 - The application shall present the user with a warning message when saving a patient’s plan fails due to a communication error with the 
database. The message should ask the user to retry after a few seconds. 

8 - The retry should succeed, and the new data should be saved.
<<<
